{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2422","id":2328404512,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz886KyKIg","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2422","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2422.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2422.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2422","number":2422,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"redo all route code","user":{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This is more of an experiment that might work out, might not.\r\n\r\nI've been worn down by how incredibly complicated our route (subnet route) and particularly HA route logic is. the database part has pointers to state that should be way out of reach (connected nodes) and so on.\r\nWe also store a bunch of info in the database that we dont need to persist:\r\n\r\n- Routes dont need its own table, it might as well just live in node.hostinfo (instead of being copied)\r\n- Approved routes can just be a prefix list on the node object, in the node table\r\n- Primary Route (HA) is only relevant at runtime, if there are two of a node, only set it for one.\r\n- CLI interface can just be overwriting, a set operation listing all approved routes for a node.\r\n\r\nBase premise:\r\n- Remove Route table and code (keep structure for migration)\r\n- Remove complex save logic trying to figure out if its HA and needs to be failed over and all at the same time as saving.\r\n- Approvals is a simple list on the node object\r\n- \"Announced\" routes are the Hostinfo.RoutableIPs minus !ApprovedRoutes\r\n- Track Primary routes \"in memory\"\r\n  - This part isnt necessarily beautiful, but I think it will be a lot simpler\r\n- these changes very seldom, so when a HA change, just send a full update\r\n  - This we can optimise later, and the new structure should fit better into an event bus of some sort.\r\n\r\nThere is gonna be part of this code which isnt particularly \"efficient\", but that can be optimised later. I doubt it would be worse than the current setup anyways. Make it work, then make it fast.\r\n\r\nTODO:\r\n- [x] Wire up Primary route tracker\r\n- [x] Delete old CLI, write new\r\n- [x] Write migration code (and test)\r\n- [x] handle autoapprovers\r\n- [x] Possibly handle exit routes after (#2444)\r\n- [x] Add changelog\r\n- [x] Update docs\r\n\r\n\r\nNew CLI should be a lot easier to reason about:\r\n\r\nList all (or specific) routes:\r\n\r\n```\r\nheadscale nodes list-routes  [-i <node_id>]\r\n```\r\n\r\nApproval of routes will overwrite all, so you define the ones you want,\r\nyou can approve routes that are not yet defined:\r\n\r\n```\r\nheadscale nodes approve-routes -i <node_id> \"comma,separated,routes\"\r\n```","created_at":"2025-02-11T10:51:19Z","updated_at":"2025-02-26T15:22:56Z","closed_at":"2025-02-26T15:22:55Z","merged_at":"2025-02-26T15:22:55Z","merge_commit_sha":"7891378f5701f4b5c31453e9cf29f6bad0e781ba","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"nblock","id":131119,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTExOQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent